cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this review-stage software/manuscript package, please cite the final archived release once the Zenodo DOI is available."
title: "Exact fiber elimination for the Levi--Civita convexity gates of the planar restricted three-body problem, with a global convexity reconnaissance"
authors:
  - family-names: Grisa
    given-names: César Augusto
    affiliation: "Universidade Federal Fluminense"
    email: cagrisa@id.uff.br
version: "1.4.0-rc1"
date-released: "2026-10-08"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/cagrisa-creator/pcr3bp-fiber-elimination"
keywords:
  - restricted three-body problem
  - Levi-Civita regularization
  - strict convexity
  - convexity gates
  - computer-assisted proof
  - numerical reconnaissance
abstract: >-
  This review-stage package accompanies a revised manuscript on exact fiber
  elimination for the Levi-Civita convexity gates of the planar circular
  restricted three-body problem. For fixed parameters, the regularized surface is
  tested over a three-dimensional domain: a two-dimensional Levi-Civita base and
  a fiber angle. The tangential gate has an exact two-variable fiber minimum,
  while the determinant gate has an exact harmonic decomposition giving a
  rigorous sufficient two-variable lower bound. The package also contains a
  numerical Earth-Moon spot check and a floating-point global reconnaissance;
  these numerical components are not interval certificates unless explicitly
  stated otherwise. A final Zenodo DOI is still pending and must be inserted
  before public release/resubmission.
